  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "The osmotic pressure of a solution of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaCl</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>10</mn></math> atm and that of a glucose solution is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>20</mn></math> atm. The osmotic pressure of a solution formed by mixing <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math> of the sodium chloride solution with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math> of the glucose solution is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> atm. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is&nbsp;________&nbsp;(nearest integer)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "167",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>iCRT</mi></math></p><p>On mixing two solution&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mi>final</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mi>final</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>500</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>100</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mi>atm</mi></math></p><p>So,&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>167</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></math></p>",
